            "thinking": "The user wants a one-sentence explanation of why the sky is blue, so I'll keep the answer to a single sentence: sunlight holds every color, and air molecules scatter the shorter blue wavelengths far more than the longer ones, which is why blue reaches our eyes from all over the sky.\n\n",
            "signature": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The sky looks blue because air molecules scatter short-wavelength blue light from sunlight far more strongly than longer-wavelength red light (Rayleigh scattering), sending that blue light toward our eyes from all directions overhead."
          }
